{'question': 'Question Text: Liam arrives at a theme park on the \( 1^{\text {st }} \) August at \( 1007 \), how long will he have there if he stays until closing time?
Question Text: \begin{tabular}{|c|} \hline Opening times: \\ \hline Jan - Mar: \( 1030-1700 \) \\ April - Jun: \( 0930-1700 \) \\ July - Sep: \( 0830-1815 \) \\ Oct - Dec: \( 0900-1630 \) \\ \hline \end{tabular}
Answer A Text: \( 7 \) hours and \( 8 \) minutes
Answer B Text: \( 10 \) hours and \( 15 \) minutes
Answer C Text: \( 8 \) hours and \( 15 \) minutes
Answer D Text: \( 8 \) hours and \( 8 \) minutes', 'correct_solution': 'Liam arrives on 1st August at 10:07. In August, the park is open from 08:30 to 18:15. He stays until closing time (18:15). To find out how long he will have there, subtract 10:07 from 18:15.\n\n18:15 - 10:07:\n- Hours: 18 - 10 = 8\n- Minutes: 15 - 7 = 8\nSo, the total time is 8 hours and 8 minutes.', 'incorrect_solution': '', 'self_correctness': 'Yes', 'self_typical_confusion': 3.0, 'self_typical_interactions': 3.0}
